# <type>(<scope>): <subject>
#
# Types:
#   feat     - A new feature
#   fix      - A bug fix
#   docs     - Documentation only changes
#   style    - Changes that do not affect the meaning of the code (white-space, formatting, etc)
#   refactor - A code change that neither fixes a bug nor adds a feature
#   perf     - A code change that improves performance
#   test     - Adding missing tests or correcting existing tests
#   build    - Changes that affect the build system or external dependencies
#   ci       - Changes to CI configuration files and scripts
#   chore    - Other changes that don't modify src or test files
#   revert   - Reverts a previous commit
#
# Scopes (examples):
#   home, about, work, contacts, footer, navbar, bee-support, hamburger
#   animations, styling, types, config, deps, ci, scripts
#
# Subject:
#   - Use imperative, present tense: "change" not "changed" nor "changes"
#   - Don't capitalize first letter
#   - No dot (.) at the end
#
# Body:
#   - Explain what and why vs. how
#   - Wrap at 72 characters
#
# Footer:
#   - Reference issues: "Fixes #123" or "Closes #123"
#   - Breaking changes: "BREAKING CHANGE: <description>"
#
# Examples:
#   feat(home): add hero banner animation
#   fix(navbar): resolve mobile hamburger menu toggle
#   docs(readme): update deployment instructions
#   refactor(components): extract shared button component
#   style(footer): format with prettier
#   test(home): add snapshot test for hero section
#   build(deps): update tailwindcss to v4.1.17
#   ci(github): add playwright test workflow
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------